messages:
Sam: Starting POC for NimbusCart — want to align success criteria, integration approach, and any security hurdles. Goal: chat-based returns assistant + product description generation. Need staging by next Wed.

Priya: Proposed scope: 1) embed JS SDK streaming chat into NimbusCart staging, 2) run 150-250 prompt evals (returns + product desc + edge cases), 3) initial auth via API key, prod will require customer KMS + rotated creds. Timeline: 3 weeks. Thoughts? :calendar:

Devon: For SDK streaming, recommend our Node client. Example snippet to stream chunks: 
```
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
for await (const chunk of client.chat.stream({ model: 'rwd-3b', input })) {
  // append chunk to UI
}
```
Note: client includes automatic reconnect up to 2 attempts.

Elena: Quotas for POC: can provision burst 40 req/s and 8k tokens/min. 429 returned with Retry-After header if exceeded. Recommend client backoff: exponential + jitter. We can temporarily increase if needed for dedicated test windows.

Sam: If they hit 429s during automated tests they'll fail CI. Can we do server-side fallback to a smaller model or queue requests briefly?

Priya: Yes — routing policy can fallback to rwd-1b on capacity pressure. We'll set X-Redwood-Fallback header when fallback occurs. Also can enable short queue (200ms) before rejecting for a smoother experience.

Maya: Security notes: for POC API keys are acceptable, but for prod we require customer-managed KMS integration and key rotation every 90 days. We'll provide SOC2 attestation answers and a redacted KMS integration diagram. If they want IP allowlist/VPC peering, ask for their egress ranges.

Sam: Telemetry — need per-request latency and token counts in near real-time. Do you expose those in Console or via webhook?

Priya: Console shows per-route token & latency breakdown plus traces. We can also stream webhooks for each request. Example webhook payload: {"request_id":"req_abc123","route":"/chat","tokens":182,"lat_ms":98,"model":"rwd-3b"}.

Devon: Sharing recommended retry pattern for their engs: 
```
let attempts = 0;
while (attempts < 6) {
  try { await call(); break; }
  catch (e) {
    if (e.status === 429) await sleep(expBackoff(attempts));
    else if (isTransient(e)) attempts++;
    else throw e;
  }
}
// backoff: start 250ms, max 4000ms, add jitter
```
Keep idempotency tokens for critical calls.

Elena: Also recommend keeping a session-level KV cache for chat prefixes. If they pass cached KV keys we see ~25-35% token reduction in sims. This reduces cost and pressure on quotas.

Priya: Draft success criteria for commercial signoff: 1) >=90% pass rate on eval rubric across the 200 prompt set; 2) p50 latency <120ms and p95 <350ms under expected load; 3) billing reconciliation within 5% of estimate; 4) no high-risk security items from the questionnaire. If met, sales proceeds to Dedicated sizing.

Sam: Add one more: hallucination threshold for returns flow — we need <5% hallucination on policy/Q&A prompts or flagged outputs with sources.

Priya: Will add hallucination metric (claims without verifiable attributes) to eval dashboard and run it on the prompt set. We'll also include a short prompts list to guide the model toward citation-oriented responses.

Maya: I'll upload SOC2 answers and the redacted KMS diagram this afternoon. We support configurable log retention for enterprise; include desired window in reply.

ops-bot: Action: created service account role "nimbus-poc-runner" and attached staging quota. Created at 2024-06-20T16:05:12Z.

Priya: Owners assigned: @Sam (customer lead), @Devon (SDK + sample app), @Elena (quota/SRE), @Maya (security). I'll send meeting invite for Wed 10am PST and upload the 200-prompt draft before EOD tomorrow. Devon will drop a starter repo with SDK example, eval harness (pytest), and backoff utils. :rocket:
